2026-10-15T16:52:09.0309643Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0405259Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0415013Z [0m
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0415607Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0416164Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0416490Z 
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0416774Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0417869Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0418366Z 
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0418723Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0419291Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0419584Z 
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0420242Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0420977Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0421464Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0421811Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0421977Z 
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0422147Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0422384Z 
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0422569Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0422934Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0423072Z 
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0423188Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0423341Z 
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0428790Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0429543Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0429780Z 
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0429890Z I will:
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0430019Z 
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0430189Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0430575Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0430984Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0431363Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0431658Z  - install Nix in to /nix
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0431949Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0432337Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0432818Z    /root
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0443250Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0443964Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0453895Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0454958Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0455212Z 
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0455981Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0456473Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0472926Z 
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0473634Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0486535Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0487638Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0491475Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0492041Z 
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0492484Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0492954Z 
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0493282Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0493945Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0494273Z 
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0494385Z If you would like to
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0494654Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0495050Z 
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0495313Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0495816Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-15T16:52:09.0496019Z 
